-- title:
--   Node ring generates the full-level field over the constants
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$, and let $F := \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ be the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ obtained by base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$, where $H \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$, with $F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q} \hookrightarrow F$. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq F$ such that the compositum of $F_0$ with $k_0(\overline{\mathbb Q})$, the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is all of $F$, and such that the following holds: for every intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to F$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with $k_0(K')$, if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ in $F$, then every $a_i = 0$. Let $O$ be a subring of $F_0$ such that every $f \in F_0$ can be written $f h = g$ with $g, h \in O$, $h \neq 0$, and let $\mathcal N_0$ be a subring of $F$ whose elements are exactly the $f \in F$ that lie in $F_0$ and whose corresponding element of $F_0$ lies in $O$. The conclusion is that for every $f \in F$ there are $n$, scalars $c_i \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$, elements $a_i \in \mathcal N_0$ and $b \in \mathcal N_0$ with $b \neq 0$ in $F$ and $f b = \sum_i c_i \cdot a_i$, the sum taken with the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-scalar action on $F$.
--
--   This is the clause asserting that a subring $O$ with fraction field $F_0$, read inside the full-level function field $F$, generates $F$ over the constant field $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ up to denominators from the ring itself. It is used in the assembly of layered rational node rings, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layeredRationalNodeRings_of_node_ends_layers`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_layeredRationalNodeRings_of_node_ends_layers) and its prime variant.
